WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:06.149
Guardians of the Galaxy Volume 2 is here,
and once again, Groot has stolen the show

00:00:06.149 --> 00:00:10.269
— this time as a pint-sized sapling of his
former self.

00:00:10.269 --> 00:00:14.330
After the first film, it's easy to assume
you might know everything there is to know

00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:16.230
about this talking tree.

00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:21.750
But Groot's roots run deep, and there are
more than a few buried secrets fans might

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:24.820
not know about Groot and his many forms.

00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:26.870
I speak for the trees

00:00:26.870 --> 00:00:32.920
Vin Diesel, the voice of Groot, is getting
a nice payday just to say the same three words

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:34.250
over and over…

00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:35.420
"I am Groot."

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:41.609
...but part of the skill involved is saying
those three words with emotion.

00:00:41.609 --> 00:00:42.480
"I…

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:43.360
AM…

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:45.600
GROOOOT!"

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:50.480
One of the film's running themes is that Groot
is actually having a complex conversation

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:52.920
with those who can to understand him, like
Rocket.

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:54.940
So, where does that leave Diesel?

00:00:54.940 --> 00:00:58.740
"I AM GROOOOOT!"

00:00:59.390 --> 00:01:03.720
He's confirmed that he actually works from
a secret script with real dialogue, which

00:01:03.729 --> 00:01:08.840
means everything that Groot utters actually
has a very literal meaning behind it.

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:13.340
You just need to be Diesel, writer-director
James Gunn, or a space raccoon in order to

00:01:13.340 --> 00:01:14.340
figure it out.

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:19.360
And while Vin Diesel has built a career out
of playing badasses, it caught some by surprise

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:25.250
when he played the voice of a CGI tree — and
later, the even higher voice of a tinier version

00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:26.570
of that tree.

00:01:26.570 --> 00:01:27.600
Even more surprising?

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:32.930
Baby Groot's voice is almost completely Diesel,
with very little voice modulation.

00:01:32.930 --> 00:01:34.680
"I am groot."

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:38.680
In an interview with Entertainment Tonight,
Diesel revealed that he'd been practicing

00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:42.410
copying the voices of cartoon characters from
a very young age.

00:01:42.410 --> 00:01:48.530
Diesel just happens to be right at home doing
silly voices on command, so he had no trouble

00:01:48.530 --> 00:01:50.550
voicing Baby Groot naturally.

00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:52.410
Say what?

00:01:52.410 --> 00:01:58.450
Groot is mostly known for his three magic
words: "I am Groot."

00:01:58.450 --> 00:02:02.530
But during his early comic appearances, Groot
was much more talkative.

00:02:02.530 --> 00:02:03.930
So what happened?

00:02:03.930 --> 00:02:08.840
According to one possible theory presented
by Marvel, Groot's race all have a weirdly

00:02:08.840 --> 00:02:14.780
specific condition: their larynx hardens as
they get older, leaving them only capable

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:16.760
of emitting a handful of words.

00:02:16.760 --> 00:02:22.689
While Baby Groot retains his tiny vocal vocabulary
in the sequel, comics lore says that he might

00:02:22.689 --> 00:02:25.700
have been able to say a lot more.

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:27.170
He's a real-life hero

00:02:27.170 --> 00:02:32.849
While it wasn't the original intent behind
Groot, he's a pretty logical mascot for ecological

00:02:32.849 --> 00:02:33.849
causes.

00:02:33.849 --> 00:02:35.290
The guy's a freakin' tree, after all.

00:02:35.290 --> 00:02:37.680
As it turns out, Disney agrees.

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:43.510
Under Disney's guidance, YouTuber D-trix created
a dance move inspired by a dancing Baby Groot

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:44.300
toy.

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:45.540
"YEAH!"

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:58.180
For each Marvel fan who used the hashtag #GrootDanceBomb
between April 18th and May 5th, or simply

00:02:58.180 --> 00:03:03.250
liked or shared the original video, Disney
donated one dollar to the Nature Conservancy,

00:03:03.250 --> 00:03:06.209
up to $250,000.

00:03:06.209 --> 00:03:11.529
Baby Groot didn't just help save the galaxy
— his dance moves are helping save planet

00:03:11.529 --> 00:03:12.760
Earth, too.

00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:14.769
New twist on old roots

00:03:14.769 --> 00:03:20.550
As a twig-sized tot, Baby Groot's personality
has changed from his first film appearance.

00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:23.680
He's now a "baby" in more than just name.

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:29.110
The movie implies that his intelligence and
personality revolve around his relative age,

00:03:29.110 --> 00:03:34.669
something which is made explicit with Groot's
appearance as a surly teenager during a mid-credits

00:03:34.669 --> 00:03:35.669
scene.

00:03:35.669 --> 00:03:40.430
However, this idea of Groot's changing personality
isn't from the comics, where he's had to regrow

00:03:40.430 --> 00:03:41.980
a number of times.

00:03:41.980 --> 00:03:46.599
As far as comics are concerned, Groot can
grow back from even a tiny sliver.

00:03:46.599 --> 00:03:51.569
And when he does, he still has all of adult
Groot's memories, so he doesn't go through

00:03:51.569 --> 00:03:53.690
any prolonged re-learning phase.

00:03:53.690 --> 00:03:58.829
And even if he did, it would probably be moot:
the Groot of the comics usually grows much

00:03:58.829 --> 00:04:03.499
faster than movie Groot, who's taken a bit
of time to go from potted plant to toddler

00:04:03.499 --> 00:04:04.499
tree.

00:04:04.499 --> 00:04:06.059
Roots of aggression

00:04:06.059 --> 00:04:10.480
One of the interesting side effects of Groot
being re-grown is that the younger version

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:13.920
seems more aggressive than his former, elder
self.

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:18.810
Sure, Groot could fight when he had to, but
Baby Groot takes to battle with zeal.

00:04:18.810 --> 00:04:21.560
But is it really that much of a surprise?

00:04:21.560 --> 00:04:26.379
In his earliest comics appearances, Groot
was a different kind of monster — tall,

00:04:26.379 --> 00:04:28.630
broad, articulate, and evil.

00:04:28.630 --> 00:04:33.960
He tried to take over Earth, and he posed
just as much of a threat as any Marvel villain,

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:38.289
but as he got older, he mellowed out and became
a hero.

00:04:38.289 --> 00:04:44.319
Baby Groot's unexpectedly violent mood swings
may be just because he's in his tree-equivalent

00:04:44.319 --> 00:04:49.830
of the terrible twos, but they also could
be from James Gunn channeling Groot's pulpy

00:04:49.830 --> 00:04:50.830
origins.

00:04:50.830 --> 00:04:54.540
Whatever the reason, the tiny tree practically
stole the show.

00:04:54.540 --> 00:04:58.140
And in a movie with this many weirdos, that's
saying something.

00:04:59.920 --> 00:05:00.480
"Oh, wow."

00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:00.990
"Yeah, I know.

00:05:00.990 --> 00:05:02.229
That almost hit me."

00:05:02.229 --> 00:05:03.229
Thanks for watching!

00:05:03.229 --> 00:05:05.789
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:05.789 --> 00:05:08.529
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

